  "chapter": {
    "number": 3,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "A Psalm of David, when he fled from the presence of his son Abessalom."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O Lord, why are they that afflict me multiplied? many rise up against me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Many say concerning my soul, There is no deliverance for him in his God.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 5
          },
          {
            "text": "Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But you, O Lord, are my helper: my glory, and the one that lifts up my head.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I cried to the Lord with my voice, and he heard me out of his holy mountain. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I lay down and slept; I awaked; for the Lord will help me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will not be afraid of ten thousands of people, who beset me round about.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Arise, Lord; deliver me, my God: for you have struck all who were without cause my enemies; you have broken the teeth of sinners.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Deliverance is the Lord's, and your blessing is upon your people.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 5,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "The word Διάψαλμα (Selah) has been rendered Pause, as most intelligible to the English reader.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 3,
          "verse": 2
        }
      }
    ]
